    <section class="nexus-edge-sec-2">
      <div class="wrap">

        <div class="nexus-edge-architecture-header">

          <p class="eyebrow">
            Architecture
          </p>

          <h2 id="boomdevs_6" class="nexus-edge-architecture-heading">
            Your autonomous desktop ally for<br>
            continuous resolution
          </h2>

        </div>

        <div class="nexus-edge-card-slider">

                      
            <div class="nexus-edge-card-slide" data-card="0">
              <div class="nexus-edge-card-frame">

                <div class="nexus-edge-card-visual">

                  <img loading="lazy" class="nexus-edge-card-image nexus-edge-card-image-small"
                    src="https://yellow.ai/wp-content/themes/yellow.ai/img/v2/cloud-brain-visual-small.webp" alt="" aria-hidden="true" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                    width="191" height="274">

                  <img loading="lazy" class="nexus-edge-card-image nexus-edge-card-image-expanded"
                    src="https://yellow.ai/wp-content/themes/yellow.ai/img/v2/cloud-brain-visual-expanded.webp" alt="Diagram: the cloud Nexus Agent orchestrating across knowledge base, identity, ITSM and backend apps down to Nexus EDGE on the desktop"
                    loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="596" height="322">

                </div>

                <div class="nexus-edge-card-copy">

                  <p class="nexus-edge-card-label">One cloud brain</p>

                  <h3 id='edge-thinks-with-your-enterprise-stack'  id="boomdevs_7" class="nexus-edge-card-title" >EDGE thinks with your enterprise stack</h3>

                  <p class="nexus-edge-card-text">The cloud Nexus Agent orchestrates across multiple LLMs, grounded in your knowledge base, SOPs, identity system, and the backend applications your work actually runs on. Remediation logic is served live, never frozen in a wiki article from six months ago. It&#039;s the same backbone that powers Nexus across CX and EX.</p>

                </div>

              </div>
            </div>

                      
            <div class="nexus-edge-card-slide" data-card="1">
              <div class="nexus-edge-card-frame">

                <div class="nexus-edge-card-visual">

                  <img loading="lazy" class="nexus-edge-card-image nexus-edge-card-image-small"
                    src="https://yellow.ai/wp-content/themes/yellow.ai/img/v2/desktop-runtime-visual-small.webp" alt="" aria-hidden="true" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                    width="191" height="274">

                  <img loading="lazy" class="nexus-edge-card-image nexus-edge-card-image-expanded"
                    src="https://yellow.ai/wp-content/themes/yellow.ai/img/v2/desktop-runtime-visual-expanded.webp" alt="Screenshot: a completed device.printers tool call showing its arguments and result"
                    loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="596" height="322">

                </div>

                <div class="nexus-edge-card-copy">

                  <p class="nexus-edge-card-label">One desktop runtime</p>

                  <h3 id='the-fix-runs-on-the-actual-device'  id="boomdevs_8" class="nexus-edge-card-title" >The fix runs on the actual device</h3>

                  <p class="nexus-edge-card-text">EDGE is built on computer-use capability, native to the desktop. It sees the same screen the user sees and runs fixes locally on the device, without opening a remote control session. Common L1 issues resolve in under a minute.</p>

                </div>

              </div>
            </div>

                      
            <div class="nexus-edge-card-slide" data-card="2">
              <div class="nexus-edge-card-frame">

                <div class="nexus-edge-card-visual">

                  <img loading="lazy" class="nexus-edge-card-image nexus-edge-card-image-small"
                    src="https://yellow.ai/wp-content/themes/yellow.ai/img/v2/identity-boundary-visual-small.webp" alt="" aria-hidden="true" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                    width="191" height="274">

                  <img loading="lazy" class="nexus-edge-card-image nexus-edge-card-image-expanded"
                    src="https://yellow.ai/wp-content/themes/yellow.ai/img/v2/identity-boundary-visual-expanded.webp" alt="Screenshot: an approval prompt for a browser.open tool call, with Deny and Allow buttons"
                    loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="596" height="322">

                </div>

                <div class="nexus-edge-card-copy">

                  <p class="nexus-edge-card-label">One identity boundary</p>

                  <h3 id='every-action-stays-inside-the-user-039-s-permissions'  id="boomdevs_9" class="nexus-edge-card-title" >Every action stays inside the user&#039;s permissions</h3>

                  <p class="nexus-edge-card-text">Every action EDGE takes runs inside the signed-in user&#039;s RBAC, audit-logged across IT, HR, and Ops as it happens. Actions are reversible by default. No shadow access, no off-RBAC pathways.</p>

                </div>

              </div>
            </div>

          
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="nexus-edge-sec-3">
      <div class="wrap">

        <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-header">

          <p class="eyebrow">
            What makes EDGE different?
          </p>

          <h2 id="boomdevs_10" class="nexus-edge-comparison-heading">
            Employee help tools stop one step<br>
            short of the fix
          </h2>

          <p class="nexus-edge-comparison-description">
            Every tool in the stack can find the fix. None of them can perform it.
          </p>

        </div>
        <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-grid">
          <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-column">
            <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-title nexus-edge-comparison-title-left">
              The way employee help tools are built today:
            </div>
            <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-list">
              <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-item">
                <span class="nexus-edge-comparison-marker"></span>
                <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-item-content">
                  <h3 id='4-fragmented-tools'  id="boomdevs_11" >4 fragmented tools</h3>
                  <p>
                    Portal, chat, KB, and remote support cobbled together.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-item">
                <span class="nexus-edge-comparison-marker"></span>

                <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-item-content">
                  <h3 id='endless-triage-cycles'  id="boomdevs_12" >Endless triage cycles</h3>

                  <p>
                    Ticket → route → link article → user does manual work.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-item">
                <span class="nexus-edge-comparison-marker"></span>

                <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-item-content">
                  <h3 id='blind-to-live-device-state'  id="boomdevs_13" >Blind to live device state</h3>

                  <p>
                    No context on running apps, screen context, or active errors.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-item">
                <span class="nexus-edge-comparison-marker"></span>

                <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-item-content">
                  <h3 id='risky-opaque-execution'  id="boomdevs_14" >Risky &amp; opaque execution</h3>

                  <p>
                    Ticketing tools can’t safely interact with local user screens.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-item">
                <span class="nexus-edge-comparison-marker"></span>

                <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-item-content">
                  <h3 id='fragmented-logs'  id="boomdevs_15" >Fragmented logs</h3>

                  <p>
                    Isolated logs across systems with zero reconciliation.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-column">
            <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-title nexus-edge-comparison-title-right">
              The way Nexus Edge is built
            </div>
            <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-list">

              <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-item">
                <span class="nexus-edge-comparison-marker"></span>

                <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-item-content">
                  <h3 id='one-unified-engine'  id="boomdevs_16" >One unified engine</h3>

                  <p>
                    Single desktop app replacing the entire support stack.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-item">
                <span class="nexus-edge-comparison-marker"></span>

                <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-item-content">
                  <h3 id='instant-resolution'  id="boomdevs_17" >Instant resolution</h3>

                  <p>
                    Perceives, reasons, executes, and audits in one real-time flow.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-item">
                <span class="nexus-edge-comparison-marker"></span>

                <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-item-content">
                  <h3 id='live-screen-awareness'  id="boomdevs_18" >Live screen awareness</h3>

                  <p>
                    Reads local apps, screen context, and error states natively.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-item">
                <span class="nexus-edge-comparison-marker"></span>

                <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-item-content">
                  <h3 id='human-in-the-loop-control'  id="boomdevs_19" >Human-in-the-loop control</h3>

                  <p>
                    Users approve every action; always bound by local RBAC.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-item">
                <span class="nexus-edge-comparison-marker"></span>

                <div class="nexus-edge-comparison-item-content">
                  <h3 id='single-source-of-truth'  id="boomdevs_20" >Single source of truth</h3>

                  <p>
                    Unified audit trail across IT, HR, and Ops written live.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

            </div>

          </div>

        </div>

      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="nexus-edge-sec-4">
      <div class="wrap">

        <div class="nexus-edge-use-cases-header">

          <p class="eyebrow">
            Use cases
          </p>

          <h2 id="boomdevs_21" class="nexus-edge-use-cases-heading">
            How EDGE works, on three real desktops
          </h2>

        </div>

        <div class="nexus-edge-use-cases">

          <!-- Use case 1 -->

          <article class="nexus-edge-use-case">

            <div class="nexus-edge-use-case-content">

              <div class="nexus-edge-use-case-icon">
                <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://yellow.ai/wp-content/themes/yellow.ai/img/v2/perception-icon.svg" alt=""
                  width="30" height="30">
              </div>

              <h3 id="boomdevs_22" class="nexus-edge-use-case-title">
                Perception
              </h3>

              <p class="nexus-edge-use-case-lead">
                A designer’s laptop has been slow for a week, and nobody knows why.
              </p>

              <p class="nexus-edge-use-case-text">
                EDGE scanned the machine and surfaced the OS version, a pending
                update, and something nobody asked about: memory running at near
                capacity.
              </p>

              <p class="nexus-edge-use-case-note">
                The employee asked about updates. EDGE found the actual root cause.
              </p>

            </div>

                        <div class="nexus-edge-use-case-visual">
              <div class="nexus-edge-use-case-frame">
                <video class="nexus-edge-use-case-video" muted loop playsinline preload="none"
