            </div>

          </article>


          <!-- Use case 2 -->

          <article class="nexus-edge-use-case nexus-edge-use-case-reverse">

                        <div class="nexus-edge-use-case-visual">
              <div class="nexus-edge-use-case-frame">
                <video class="nexus-edge-use-case-video" muted loop playsinline preload="none"
                  poster="https://yellow.ai/wp-content/themes/yellow.ai/img/v2/use-case-context.webp"
                  aria-label="Nexus Edge context interface" disablepictureinpicture>
                  <source src="https://yellow.ai/wp-content/themes/yellow.ai/img/v2/Context.webm"
                    type="video/mp4">
                  <img loading="lazy" src="https://yellow.ai/wp-content/themes/yellow.ai/img/v2/use-case-context.webp"
                    alt="Nexus Edge context interface" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
                </video>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="nexus-edge-use-case-content">

              <div class="nexus-edge-use-case-icon">
                <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://yellow.ai/wp-content/themes/yellow.ai/img/v2/perception-icon.svg" alt=""
                  width="30" height="30">
              </div>

              <h3 id="boomdevs_23" class="nexus-edge-use-case-title">
                Context
              </h3>

              <p class="nexus-edge-use-case-lead">
                9:10 a.m. Two tickets are open, both marked medium, with no
                indication of which comes first.
              </p>

              <p class="nexus-edge-use-case-text">
                EDGE asked whether to scope the list to this employee alone,
                opened the work tracker, applied the assignee filter, and read
                back both tickets with status, priority, and customer before
                recommending which to start.
              </p>

              <p class="nexus-edge-use-case-note">
                Grounded in the systems of record the company already uses, EDGE
                didn’t answer from a generic knowledge article. It went and checked.
              </p>

            </div>

          </article>


          <!-- Use case 3 -->

          <article class="nexus-edge-use-case">

            <div class="nexus-edge-use-case-content">

              <div class="nexus-edge-use-case-icon">
                <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://yellow.ai/wp-content/themes/yellow.ai/img/v2/perception-icon.svg" alt=""
                  width="30" height="30">
              </div>

              <h3 id="boomdevs_24" class="nexus-edge-use-case-title">
                Execution
              </h3>

              <p class="nexus-edge-use-case-lead">
                An urgent document from Finance is due, but the printer is stuck.
              </p>

              <p class="nexus-edge-use-case-text">
                EDGE identified the suspended printer queue, flagged the
                state-changing action, and displayed the exact command before
                executing. The employee selected Allow, and printing resumed
                strictly within their existing permissions.
              </p>

              <p class="nexus-edge-use-case-note">
                No privilege escalation and no autonomous takeover. EDGE keeps
                every action transparent and employee-approved.
              </p>

            </div>

                        <div class="nexus-edge-use-case-visual">
              <div class="nexus-edge-use-case-frame">
                <video class="nexus-edge-use-case-video" muted loop playsinline preload="none"
